  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Deloitte and Touche recorded $461M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Deloitte and Touche won 156 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $3M. Obligations fell 31.1% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations climbed from $384M in FY21 to a peak of $734M in FY23, then declined to $669M in FY25 and now sit at $461M for FY26 to date. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $193M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $95.3M and the Department of Homeland Security at $37M. Other Computer Related Services is the single largest market for Deloitte and Touche work at $357M, with Other Accounting Services the next largest at $74.3M. Offices of Certified Public Accountants and Custom Computer Programming Services also appear among the top markets. The FY2026 to date totals are partial and represent obligations recorded so far in the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did Deloitte and Touche's obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 31.1% year over year. Deloitte and Touche obligated $461M in FY2026 to date after reaching $669M in FY25 and $734M in FY23. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $384M in FY21 to $734M in FY23 before trending down to the current FY26 level. The current-year total is partial and covers the fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and which markets dominate Deloitte and Touche work?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $193M. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $95.3M, the Department of Homeland Security obligated $37M, and other top buyers include the Department of the Treasury at $30.8M and the Social Security Administration at $25.5M. Other Computer Related Services is the largest market at $357M, followed by Other Accounting Services at $74.3M and Offices of Certified Public Accountants at $15.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
